# Every value here is OPTIONAL and every one is a PUBLIC client identifier.
# An absent value disables its feature quietly; the app opens either way.
# 🔴 No server secret belongs in a VITE_ variable - the bundler inlines it.

# Telemetry. 🔴 The KEY is the only condition - there is no consent flag to read.
# The owner removed the opt-out on 2026-09-07: the first-run screen is a notice,
# not a question, so a gate here would be a control nobody can reach. A value
# present means that destination is live from the first boot. Owner row 16.
#
# 🔴 These are FOUR destinations, not one switch, and configuredFeatures() now
# answers per destination for exactly that reason. It used to return a single
# boolean that was true if ANY key was set - so a build with only a Sentry DSN
# reported "telemetry: configured" while GA4, Amplitude and Clarity received
# nothing, and the Privacy tab's "no destination is configured" sentence
# disappeared while three of the four were still dark. Fill them together, or
# know which one is missing.
#
# All four are GitHub repository VARIABLES on aoneahsan/windowsweep (not secrets -
# every one of them is a public client identifier that ships in the bundle by
# design). A clone without them still builds and simply sends nothing.
#
#   VITE_GA4_MEASUREMENT_ID   G-XXXXXXXXXX      screen views and control presses
#   VITE_AMPLITUDE_API_KEY    32 hex characters the same events, in a second tool
#   VITE_CLARITY_PROJECT_ID   10 characters     session replay, all text masked
#   VITE_SENTRY_DSN           https://...       crash reports, paths scrubbed
VITE_GA4_MEASUREMENT_ID=
VITE_AMPLITUDE_API_KEY=
VITE_CLARITY_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=

# Supabase - the backend, since 2026-09-05. Both values come from the FilesHub
# vault; the publishable key is PUBLIC by design and its whole security model is
# RLS. 🔴 The secret key belongs nowhere near this file.
#
# The project exists and its schema is applied (ref nlmetjyytgwaxcliusuo, created
# 2026-09-07). These two are STILL DELIBERATELY EMPTY, and the reason is not the
# database:
#
# 🔴 Google is the only sign-in this app offers, and it is not enabled on the
#    project - `GET /auth/v1/settings` reports `external.google: false`. Filling
#    these in would make `configuredFeatures()` advertise sign-in and sync, and
#    the button would then fail on press against an unconfigured provider. An app
#    that reports a feature as unconfigured is better than one that offers it and
#    breaks, so these wait on MANUAL-TASKS row 15 - a Google Web OAuth client
#    whose authorised redirect URI is
#    `https://nlmetjyytgwaxcliusuo.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback`, entered in
#    Supabase's own Auth -> Providers form. The app never sees that id or secret.
#
# Nothing else is blocked by this: every cleanup feature works signed out, and
# the engine makes no network calls at all.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
